provider_responses.text:
The key next step is to move from proving theories about your identity to tracking concrete recovery.

For the next week, focus on:

- consistent sleep, food, hydration, movement, and lower stimulation;
- one ordinary task and one human contact each day;
- brief symptom notes: sleep, anxiety, detachment, mood, functioning;
- no late-night or repeated “am I permanently changed?” analysis;
- delay major conclusions about what the experience means.

Use this sentence when the loop starts:

> “This is a state, not a verdict. I will stabilize first and interpret later.”

If symptoms are persistent, worsening, or affecting safety, sleep, work, self-care, or reality-testing, contact a licensed mental-health professional or urgent support service.

